  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "The sun hangs low over the Hearth, casting long shadows across the Market square. The air is thick with the scent of fresh bread from the bakery, and the distant sound of the mill's wheel turning. Ash and Wren stand in the square, their faces etched with concern.", "cited_fact_keys": ["place", "spots"]},
